8dbe5fca6d940f20324097245344bb81a0488f43ef1b2b35dcf2a7ed8c67ea84{"version":1,"source":{"accession":"0000072903-26-000149","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-07-30","cik":"0000072903","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/72903/000007290326000149/xcelearningsreleaseq22026.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/eb943d10a7fcdd3ce87f2d413d140c5f1709b7862b0d4f8b73d8060527432252.bin","sha256":"eb943d10a7fcdd3ce87f2d413d140c5f1709b7862b0d4f8b73d8060527432252"},"layers":{"businessProfile":{"status":"no_evidence","evidence":[],"omittedEvidenceCount":0},"operatingKpis":{"status":"evidence_available","evidence":[{"id":"34ce71dbe86a3794be9143d65454877a452c387e44afc8a9989a7230daea5006","quote":"NSP System — Resource Acquisition — In December 2025, NSP-Minnesota and NSP-Wisconsin jointly issued a Request for Proposal (RFP) seeking up to 3,500 MW of wind, solar, hydro, standalone storage, or hybrid capacity that will achieve commercial operation by December 31, 2030. Short-listed projects were announced in June 2026, and filing for requisite regulatory approval is expected by the end of 2026.","context":"NSP-Minnesota — 2026 North Dakota Natural Gas Rate Case — In January 2026, NSP-Minnesota filed a natural gas rate case in North Dakota, for an annual rate increase of $14 million (11.9%). The filing is based on a 2026 forecast test year and includes an ROE of 10.85%, a 52.5% equity ratio and rate base of $235 million. In March 2026, the North Dakota Public Service Commission approved interim rates of $12 million effective April 1, 2026. The procedural schedule is yet to be determined.","section":"","block":123,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000072903-26-000149","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-07-30","cik":"0000072903","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/72903/000007290326000149/xcelearningsreleaseq22026.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/eb943d1